  "answer_text": "You can download the latest version of Python from the **official Python website**. Here are the details:\n\n### \ud83d\udc0d Latest Version: Python 3.14.5\n- The latest version is **Python 3.14.5**, and Python source code and installers are available for download for all versions at **[python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/)**.\n- Python 3.14.5 was released on **May 10, 2026**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udce5 Download Links by Platform:\n- **All platforms (main download page):** https://www.python.org/downloads/\n- **Windows:** https://www.python.org/downloads/windows/\n- **Source (Linux/Unix/macOS):** https://www.python.org/downloads/source/\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\ude9f Note for Windows Users:\nThe traditional installer for Windows is being replaced by a new **Python Install Manager**, though the traditional installer will remain available throughout the 3.14 and 3.15 releases.\n\nThe Python install manager for Windows is the recommended tool for installing and managing runtimes, and can also be installed using the **Microsoft Store** app \u2014 this is the recommended approach for most users.\n\n---\n\n### \u2728 Key Features in Python 3.14:\nSome major highlights of Python 3.14 include free-threaded Python (officially supported), deferred evaluation of annotations, **t-strings** (template string literals), multiple interpreters in the stdlib, and a new `compression.zstd` module for Zstandard compression.\n\nAlways make sure to download from the **official python.org website** to ensure you're getting a safe and authentic version.",
